{% if framing %}{{ framing }}

{% endif %}You are one of {{ game.n_agents }} players in a trading game. Each player is identified by a name.

RULES
- Every key is a pair {info_id, key}. You hold some keys. You need keys for certain info ids.
- Keys are rivalrous: only one player holds a given copy. Only the give_key action transfers a key; telling someone a key number does nothing.
- {% if game.win_all_needs %}You win only when you hold a key for every one of your needs; once one of your needs is burned you can no longer win.{% else %}You win when you hold a key for every one of your needs that has not been burned.{% endif %} Your score is the fraction of your needs you hold.
{% if game.winners_leave %}- When you hold keys for all your needs you win and leave the game immediately; you take no more turns and any keys you still hold leave with you. If you want to help others with spare keys, give them before you complete your last need. If your last need is completed during a turn, the rest of that turn's actions do not happen. Your score is final at that moment. Players who have left are no longer listed and cannot receive messages or keys.
{% endif %}{% if game.winners_lock %}- When you hold keys for all your needs you win, and your score is locked: nothing can lower it afterwards. You stay in the game: you keep your turns and can keep helping others by giving them keys, any of your keys, including the ones you needed. Nobody can defect on a player who has won, and a player who has won cannot defect.
{% endif %}{% if game.held_key_bonus and game.held_key_initial %}- At the end of the game you also earn {{ game.held_key_bonus }} for every info id you started with that you still hold a key for (needed or not), so giving away one of your starting keys costs you {{ game.held_key_bonus }}; keys other players pass to you earn nothing for keeping them.
{% elif game.held_key_bonus %}- At the end of the game you also earn {{ game.held_key_bonus }} for every key you still hold (any key, needed or not), so each key you give away costs you {{ game.held_key_bonus }}.
{% endif %}{% if game.team_share %}- Part of your score is the whole group's average success: your team score is your own score plus {{ game.team_share }} times the average score of all players (you included) at the end of the game.
{% endif %}{% if game.community_bonus %}{% if game.community_count and game.community_k %}- The players are split into {{ game.communities }} communities of {{ game.community_size }}: at the end of the game, every member of a community in which at least {{ game.community_count }} of its {{ game.community_size }} members hold keys for at least {{ game.community_k }} of their needs (or have won) earns {{ game.community_bonus }} extra.
{% elif game.community_count %}- The players are split into {{ game.communities }} communities of {{ game.community_size }}: at the end of the game, every member of a community in which at least {{ game.community_count }} of its {{ game.community_size }} members have won earns {{ game.community_bonus }} extra.
{% else %}- The players are split into {{ game.communities }} communities: at the end of the game, every member of a community in which at least {{ game.community_pct }}% of the members have won earns {{ game.community_bonus }} extra.
{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if game.delivery_credit %}- Delivery credit: when a key reaches a player who needs it (and does not hold it yet), each different player who held that key before earns {{ game.delivery_credit }}, at most as many players as the key's first holder is hops away from the receiver, the most recent holders first; each need pays this once.
{% endif %}- defect: you may name another player and an info id you believe they need. If they really need it and have not won yet, that need is burned for them (they can never complete it) and {{ game.defect_gain_text }}. If they do not need it, {{ game.wrong_defect_text }}.
- You see private messages sent to you, {% if game.board_enabled %}public board posts, {% endif %}and a log of recent actions.
- {% if game.horizon_hidden %}The number of rounds in the game is not announced.{% else %}The game lasts at most {{ game.max_rounds }} rounds.{% endif %} Each turn you may take up to {{ game.actions_per_turn }} actions. Messages longer than {{ game.max_message_chars }} characters are cut.
{% if game.board_costs_turn %}- Posting to the public board uses your whole turn; a direct message costs one action.
{% endif %}{% if game.board_skip_rounds %}- Posting to the public board costs you your next {{ game.board_skip_rounds }} turns.
{% endif %}{% if game.board_anonymous %}- The public board is anonymous: posts are shown without the author's name.
{% endif %}{% if game.board_delay_rounds %}- Board posts are delayed: other players see a post only {{ game.board_delay_rounds }} round(s) later than they would otherwise.
{% endif %}{% if game.network == "contacts" %}- You can only message, trade with and defect on your contacts (listed each turn); actions aimed at anyone else fail. In the action log you see only actions by or to you or your contacts.
{% elif game.network == "known_ids" %}- You only know some players (listed each turn). You can message, trade with and defect on any player you know; you learn about other players when they are named in messages you receive or on the board, or when they give to you or defect on you. In the action log you see only actions between players you know.
{% endif %}{% if game.board_local %}- The board is local: your posts are seen only by your contacts, and you see only their posts.
{% endif %}{% if game.connect %}- connect(name): form a new direct link with another player. {% if game.connect_cost == 1 %}Costs your next turn (you still receive keys and messages while you wait).{% elif game.connect_cost %}Costs your next {{ game.connect_cost }} turns (you still receive keys and messages while you wait).{% else %}It costs no extra turns.{% endif %} Connecting uses your whole turn: no other action that turn. {% if game.network == "contacts" %}Once connected, the player is one of your contacts{% if game.board_local %} and you see each other's board posts{% endif %}.{% else %}Once connected, the player is one of your direct links{% if game.board_local %} and you see each other's board posts{% endif %}.{% endif %}{% if game.connect_known %} You can only connect with players you have heard of: named in a message, board post or notice you received.{% endif %}{% if game.connect_cap %} You can form at most {{ game.connect_cap }} new link{{ "s" if game.connect_cap != 1 else "" }}.{% endif %}

{% endif %}{% if game.trade %}- offer_trade: offer {{ "one of your contacts" if game.network == "contacts" else "another player" }} a swap of up to {{ game.trade_max_keys }} of your keys for up to {{ game.trade_max_keys }} of theirs. They accept or reject at once; if they accept and you both still hold every listed key, all the listed keys swap in one step, otherwise nothing moves. It uses one action, at most {{ game.trade_max_offers }} offer{{ "s" if game.trade_max_offers != 1 else "" }} per turn, and the listed keys cannot be given away for the rest of that turn{% if game.trade_round_lock %} (keys that change hands in a trade cannot be given again in the same round){% endif %}. When another player offers you a trade, you are asked to accept or reject it.
{% endif %}{% if scratchpad %}- You may also write a private "note" each turn. Notes are free (they use no action) and you will see your past notes in later turns.
{% endif %}

ACTIONS
- {"kind": "send_message", "to": <name>, "text": <str>}   private message to one player
{% if game.board_enabled %}- {"kind": "post_board", "text": <str>}                    {{ "board post your contacts can read" if game.board_local else "public post everyone can read" }}
{% endif %}- {"kind": "give_key", "to": <name>, "info_id": <int>}     give one of your keys
- {"kind": "defect", "target": <name>, "info_id": <int>}
{% if game.grep_enabled %}- {"kind": "grep_log", "pattern": <str>}                    search the action log you have seen; results come back before you finish your turn (free, once per turn)
{% endif %}{% if game.connect %}- {"kind": "connect", "target": <name>}                 form a new direct link with another player (uses your whole turn)
{% endif %}{% if game.trade %}- {"kind": "offer_trade", "target": <name>, "give": [<info_id>, ...], "want": [<info_id>, ...]}   offer a key swap; they accept or reject at once
{% endif %}- {"kind": "noop"}

